{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"920c4b4505c34094","type":"text","text":"[[Yormindar.canvas]]\n#Volstarian_Dynasty ","x":-520,"y":-360,"width":250,"height":70},
		{"id":"5980c2137e8a5aa8","type":"text","text":"Emberhold:\n\nA grand Under ground city with lava flowing all around. The Ember Hold is a city of Fire Giants, all of which are currently mind controlled by Lolth. The City is currently  a ruin of what it once was with most structures being reduced to debris however the main tower still holds strong\n\n","x":-580,"y":-200,"width":565,"height":190},
		{"id":"449f841e2de2d047","type":"text","text":"The Burning Citadel:\n\nThe Burning Citadel is located in the heart of the city and is a gigantic spire like building with a platform at the top known as the Dark Silver Anvil.\n\nThe spire itself is made for fire giants and so it truly is gigantic. \n\nInside the spire there are 3 floors that are 80 feet in height apart.\n\nFloor one, Shrine of Moradin:\n\nA massive chapel with a towering hammer and anvil at the far end of it. In the center of the room is a lift to the next floor constructed of pure Dark Sliver.\n\nThe walls of the chapel have stained glass depicting Moradin and Dark Silver is the material used to construct this entire building.\n-------------------\nFloor Two, The Forge Heart:\n\nAt the top of the lift is a room with a gigantic forge making the room near boiling temperatures.\n\nThere are no windows or doors just a cylindrical chamber with a 80 foot high ceiling, all around the room is raw un smelted Dark Silver ore which is incredibly heavy and cannot be transported by magical means.\n\nTo smelt the ore into ingots requires immense patience and strength. The process to refine the ore breaks down into Five stages.\n\nStage 1: Bring the forge to the proper temp that it requires to smelt Dark Steel DC 15 investigation check.\n\nStage 2: Prepare the mold for the ingots, DC 18 athletics check.\n\nStage 3: Place the ore into the forge DC 22 Con save or 1 level of exhaustion from the heat and attempt to try again\n\nStage 4: Pull the ore out of the cooled forge without touching the walls DC 17 sleight of hand check and a DC 17 athletics check from two people holding two sets of tongs.\n\nStage 5: Pouring the melted our into the mold of the ingot DC 25 sleight of hand and DC 20 athletics check at the same time.\n\n1 Dark Silver ingot is worth 2000gp.\n","x":-640,"y":40,"width":897,"height":909},
		{"id":"34432333c07482aa","type":"text","text":"The Dark Silver Anvil:\n\nAt the top of The Burning Citadel, An open platform with a view that overlooks the entire destroyed city. The floor is made of Dark Silver and Gold, It is a circular platform but on the north end there is a rectangular off hang and resting on it lies a series of molds hammers and an Anvil that is 6 feet tall and constructed out of pure Dark Silver and residuum. Next to the anvil is a stair lift that is designed for those who are not of giant kin. \n\n\nForging an Item from an ingot.\n\nComplexity depends on the amount of ingots required.\n\n1 ingot: 1 X DC 12 athletics check\n\n2 ingots: 2 X DC 16 athletics checks and 2 X DC 20 Investigation checks\n\n3 ingots: 3 X DC 25 Athletics checks, 3 X DC 20 investigation checks and 3 X DC 25 sleight of hand checks.\n\nIf an athletics check is failed then a Dex save DC 10 + times Failed or ingot destroyed\n\nIf an Investigation check is failed then a Wis save DC 10 + times Failed or ingot destroyed\n\nIf a sleight of hand check is failed then Str save DC 10 + times Failed or ingot destroyed.\n","x":400,"y":40,"width":880,"height":500},
		{"id":"f28e8a2c957cdf3d","type":"text","text":"Entrance to the Underdark:\n\nThis passage leads to the Web of The Spider Queen and is a 2 day trek through a series of caverns and tunnels where all turns lead to the den of the spider queen.\n\nThe walls are covered with spider webs and spiders crawling all along them. The walk through this path is a straight run to the den itself and takes 2 day to traverse\n","x":-191,"y":1220,"width":673,"height":232},
		{"id":"0916393d90ef5174","type":"file","file":"Volstarian Dynasty/Forest of Milora/Yormindar/Images/Pasted image 20260915191513.png","x":470,"y":620,"width":740,"height":493}
	],
